    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d750">

                <pb facs="1516" n="1504" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg1504"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Walter S.
                            Robertson to General Marshall</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-08-10">10 August 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6753. (Team 13) Communist Party Commissioner Yeh in an informal discussion today
                    when being pressed to direct General Ho Lung to cease attacks in Tatung area
                    stated to Timberman he could send a message to Ho Lung but that it would do no
                    good, that his power of control over field commanders had practically ceased and
                    he could not stop fighting anywhere in view of widespread nature of conflicts.
                    Previously lie had stated to me he would do nothing to <pb facs="1517" n="1505"
                        xml:id="pg1505"/> stop conflict at Tatung when discussing critical situation
                    existing at Tatung.<anchor n="72" xml:id="d750-f1"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d750-f1" n="72" xml:id="d750-f1-content">
                <p>Notation on the original: “Chou [En-lai] is in same boat”.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
